Package: parametricboot
Title: Parametric Bootstrap for Fitted Regression Models
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Diogo", family = "Ribeiro",
           email = "diogo.debastos.ribeiro@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0001-2022-7072",
                       affiliation = "ESMAD, Instituto Politecnico do Porto"))
Description: Automates the parametric bootstrap for models fitted with
    'lm()', 'glm()', 'MASS::glm.nb()', 'lme4::lmer()', 'lme4::glmer()' and 'survival::coxph()'.
    New responses are simulated from the fitted model, the model is refitted
    to each of them, and the replicates are summarised as bias, standard
    error, mean squared error, coverage and confidence intervals, propagated
    to predictions, and visualised with 'ggplot2'. Cox models use the
    model-based resampling algorithm of Davison and Hinkley (1997,
    ISBN:9780521574716).
